@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-registrar`
IMPORT `g4-council-membership`
IMPORT `g4-council-work`
IMPORT `g4-conflict`
IMPORT `g4-composition`

-- g4-tests-composition.l4: tests for g4-composition.l4.  Every composed answer is also compared with the hand-wired answer of the module that
-- takes the BOOLEAN input, so a composition that drifted from the module it calls would fail here.  Expected values were decided from the
-- Hebrew of ss.19 to 29 (inputs/law.wiki lines 159 to 242) before the module was run.

§ `Tests for the composition`

§§ `Names for the cases`

seat1 MEANS `seat 1: representative of the senior occupations-regulation division of the Ministry, the chair`
seat2 MEANS `seat 2: the Registrar`
seat3 MEANS `seat 3: the Commissioner for Standards, or an employee on the Commissioner's behalf`
seat4 MEANS `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure`
seat5 MEANS `seat 5: employee of the Ministry of Environmental Protection`
seat6 MEANS `seat 6: employee of the National Fire and Rescue Authority`
seat7 MEANS `seat 7: representative of the workers' organisation with the most licence holders`
seat8 MEANS `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation`
seat9 MEANS `seat 9: representative of the organisation with the most engineers`
seat10 MEANS `seat 10: representative of the representative organisation under the Engineers and Technicians Law`
seat11 MEANS `seat 11: public representative`

-- A foreign qualification.  Fields: description | from a foreign institution | the Registrar's opinion | recognised | made conditional | condition met.
`a foreign degree whose scope and content match` MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a recognised foreign degree`                   MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a qualification from an Israeli institution`   MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "local", FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`all four matters considered`                   MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`the scope was not considered`                  MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

-- A quorate meeting that carried the proposal 3-2, a meeting without a quorum, and the consultations built on them.
`the eleven serving` MEANS LIST (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m1", TRUE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m2", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m3", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m4", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m5", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m6", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m7", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m8", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m9", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m10", FALSE), (`Serving member of the Council` OF "m11", FALSE)
`a quorate meeting, 3-2` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `the eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting without a quorum, 4-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `the eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m5")
function3 MEANS `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
`a consultation with valid advice` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST (`the Council at a meeting` OF `a quorate meeting, 3-2`))
`a consultation with advice formed without a quorum` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST (`the Council at a meeting` OF `a meeting without a quorum, 4-1`))
`a consultation never requested` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, FALSE, (JUST (`the Council at a meeting` OF `a quorate meeting, 3-2`))
`a consultation with no advice yet` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, NOTHING

§§ `Section 19(c) with sections 24 to 26`

-- The composed answer equals the hand-wired one, and the IP7 wiring works in each direction.
#ASSERT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — a foreign qualification may be recognised:` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `after the consultation` `a consultation with valid advice`
#ASSERT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — a foreign qualification may be recognised:` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `after the consultation` `a consultation with advice formed without a quorum`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — a foreign qualification may be recognised:` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `after the consultation` `a consultation never requested`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — a foreign qualification may be recognised:` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `after the consultation` `a consultation with no advice yet`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — a foreign qualification may be recognised:` `a qualification from an Israeli institution` `after the consultation` `a consultation with valid advice`

#ASSERT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — the foreign qualification was recognised:` `a recognised foreign degree` `having considered` `all four matters considered` `after the consultation` `a consultation with valid advice`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — the foreign qualification was recognised:` `a recognised foreign degree` `having considered` `the scope was not considered` `after the consultation` `a consultation with valid advice`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — the foreign qualification was recognised:` `a recognised foreign degree` `having considered` `all four matters considered` `after the consultation` `a consultation with advice formed without a quorum`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) with ss 24 to 26 — the foreign qualification was recognised:` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `having considered` `all four matters considered` `after the consultation` `a consultation with valid advice`

§§ `Sections 20, 21 and 29(b)`

-- Candidates.  Fields: holds the position | proposed | the Minister's opinion | an engineer.
`a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a candidate who holds the position only`            MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit` MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF TRUE, `proceeding ended in a conviction`

-- Seat 4, the candidate proposed: appointable unless the s.29(b) judgements both hold, or a seat condition or the s.21 bar fails.
#ASSERT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY `, regularly in a conflict being` FALSE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY `, regularly in a conflict being` TRUE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY `, regularly in a conflict being` FALSE `and the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY `, regularly in a conflict being` TRUE `and the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY `, regularly in a conflict being` FALSE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ss 20, 21 and 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`) `, regularly in a conflict being` FALSE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
-- The composed answer equals the hand-wired one.
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY (`s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` TRUE `with the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE)

§§ `Section 23(b) with section 29(b)`

-- Fields: proceedings | permanently unable | still satisfies the seat | the record's own s.29(b) flag | has not already ceased.
`a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag set`   MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag clear` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

-- The record's own flag is replaced by what g4-conflict decides from the two judgements.
#ASSERT `s 23(b) with s 29(b) — a ground for removal exists for the member with the facts` `a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag clear` `, regularly in a conflict being` TRUE `and the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) with s 29(b) — a ground for removal exists for the member with the facts` `a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag clear` `, regularly in a conflict being` TRUE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) with s 29(b) — a ground for removal exists for the member with the facts` `a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag set` `, regularly in a conflict being` FALSE `and the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member with no ground, the record's own s.29(b) flag set`

§§ `Section 29(e) with section 20`

#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat1
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat2
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat3
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat4
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat5
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat6
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat7
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat8
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat9
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat10
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` seat11

-- Interests.  Fields: whose interest | the kind | conflicts | related to the Council's functions.
`the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting` MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `the interest of the public the member represents, as a kind of interest`, TRUE, TRUE
`the member's own personal interest, conflicting`           MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `a personal interest of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE

-- A seat 7 member: the public's interest is no conflict (s.29(e)); a seat 1 member: it is.  A personal interest is a conflict in every seat.
#ASSERT NOT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat7 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat11 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`)
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat1 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`)
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat6 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`)
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat7 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the member's own personal interest, conflicting`)
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` seat1 `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the member's own personal interest, conflicting`)

§§ `Sections 22 to 25: the serving members on a day, and the saving of the Council's acts`

`no events` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- A member of a seat, appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, with the day of removal if any.  Fields: reference | seat | appointed | further terms | events | removed on.
GIVEN seat IS A `Council seat`
      reference IS A STRING
      removal IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Service record of a member of the Council`
`a Council member in` seat `with reference` reference `removed on` removal MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF reference, seat, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `no events`, removal

`a full Council, nobody removed` MEANS LIST `a Council member in` seat1 `with reference` "m1" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat2 `with reference` "m2" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat3 `with reference` "m3" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat4 `with reference` "m4" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat5 `with reference` "m5" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat6 `with reference` "m6" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat7 `with reference` "m7" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat8 `with reference` "m8" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat9 `with reference` "m9" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat10 `with reference` "m10" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat11 `with reference` "m11" `removed on` NOTHING
`a Council in which five were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them` MEANS LIST `a Council member in` seat1 `with reference` "m1" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat2 `with reference` "m2" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat3 `with reference` "m3" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat4 `with reference` "m4" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat5 `with reference` "m5" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat6 `with reference` "m6" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat7 `with reference` "m7" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat8 `with reference` "m8" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat9 `with reference` "m9" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat10 `with reference` "m10" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat11 `with reference` "m11" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1))
`a Council in which six were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them` MEANS LIST `a Council member in` seat1 `with reference` "m1" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat2 `with reference` "m2" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat3 `with reference` "m3" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat4 `with reference` "m4" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat5 `with reference` "m5" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat6 `with reference` "m6" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat7 `with reference` "m7" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat8 `with reference` "m8" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat9 `with reference` "m9" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat10 `with reference` "m10" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat11 `with reference` "m11" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1))
`a Council in which the chair and four others were removed on 2025-12-01` MEANS LIST `a Council member in` seat1 `with reference` "m1" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat2 `with reference` "m2" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat3 `with reference` "m3" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat4 `with reference` "m4" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat5 `with reference` "m5" `removed on` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)), `a Council member in` seat6 `with reference` "m6" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat7 `with reference` "m7" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat8 `with reference` "m8" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat9 `with reference` "m9" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat10 `with reference` "m10" `removed on` NOTHING, `a Council member in` seat11 `with reference` "m11" `removed on` NOTHING

-- Before anyone was appointed, nobody serves.
#ASSERT count (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) `according to` `a full Council, nobody removed`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT count (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a full Council, nobody removed`) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT count (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a Council in which five were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them`) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2025 11 30) `according to` `a Council in which five were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them`) EQUALS 11
-- The chair is the holder of seat 1, and only seat 1: exactly one serving member is the chair, none once the chair is removed.
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD m's `the member is the chair`) (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a full Council, nobody removed`)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD m's `the member is the chair`) (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a Council in which the chair and four others were removed on 2025-12-01`)) EQUALS 0

-- The saving of s.24: six serving with the chair, yes; five, no; six without the chair is no (here, six serving with the chair removed: 11 less chair and four others is six without the chair).
#ASSERT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a full Council, nobody removed`
#ASSERT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a Council in which five were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a Council in which six were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `according to` `a Council in which the chair and four others were removed on 2025-12-01`
-- The day before the removals the same Council is whole.
#ASSERT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2025 11 30) `according to` `a Council in which six were removed on 2025-12-01, the chair not among them`
